    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense is primed for a high-output day, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (77.42) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Kyle Tucker** enters today with the highest individual efficiency score, bolstered by a juicy matchup against Robert Gasser; while the park factor is slightly negative, the elite arm-skill suppression from Gasser and the #4 order placement elevate **Kyle Tucker** as our anchor. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a substantial platoon advantage against Grant Holmes, with the optimizer rewarding his high dynamic platoon rating (+14%) and favorable spot in the two-hole, making him a cornerstone of today's production stack.\n\nSecondary value resides in our outfield and middle infield, specifically **Andy Pages** (67.85) and **Gunnar Henderson** (64.95). **Andy Pages** is a primary beneficiary of the favorable pitching matchup against Gasser, providing strong value despite a neutral park. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** faces a difficult task against Framber Valdez, but our model aggressively accounts for his specific speed profile; despite a penalty for the platoon disadvantage, his elite base-running and the \"slow delivery\" factor of Valdez ensure **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start in our pursuit of scarce stolen bases. **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) also warrants attention, as he benefits from a perfect storm of a weak SP, wind blowing out, and the leadoff spot, making him an excellent source of run generation.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nasim Nunez**, whose speed profile makes him a constant threat to enter the lineup. However, **Nasim Nunez** (54.55) was narrowly edged out by the superior power-projection floors of our starting infielders. We have also opted to sit **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.94) against the elite Skenes; while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is a roster mainstay, the optimizer correctly flagged the significant SP skill penalty (-19%) as too high a hurdle for a 5x5 Roto start today. Managers should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Liam Hicks**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Sam Antonacci**; if any drop significantly in the batting order, their efficiency scores will shift, necessitating a final look at the bench before first pitch.",
